// APW-6 -- Window-boundary burst (BUGGY): "at most 3 events per day".
//
// The *intent* is a per-window (e.g. per-day) cap.  The *bug* is that the
// counter hard-resets at the window boundary (an absolute window), so an
// attacker does 3 events just before midnight and 3 more just after -- a 2x
// burst past the cap.
//
// This is a *forward-looking* sample: Dogwood's roadmap lists absolute-time
// windows, but they are not in the language yet, so this does not lower to a
// ROTN shape.  The hand-written oracle (rot.shapes.build_window_boundary_ir)
// models the hard reset and is what ROTN decides: VIOLATED, witness
// count=1, total=4.
//
// See: docs/apw-catalog.md (APW-6), tests/test_apw6.py.

@id("apw6_buggy")
forbid (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Send",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (sum 1 for (t: Timepoint). where (
        formerly within 1d (Drupe::Action::"Send"::request{} && tp(t))
    )) > 3
};
